  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY NIGHT THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 1237 AM CST Wed Nov 11 2026\n\nA closed upper low will be centered over the Great Lakes\nThursday night with a large upper trough across the Eastern\nCONUS. This upper trough will lift into the eastern Great Lakes\nand New England by Saturday, as a negatively tilted upper trough\ndigs from the Pacific Northwest into the Central and Southern\nRockies. By Saturday night, a closed low is forecast to develop\nover the Texas panhandle with showers developing across western\nKansas and eastern Colorado. Shower chances will increase across\nthe southern half of the forecast area. Rainfall amounts look\nlight from a trace up to 0.05 inch. On Sunday, shower chance\nlinger into the morning as the closed upper low moves east near\nthe KS/OK border. The bulk of the showers will remain to our\nsouth across Kansas. \n\nHighs Friday will range from the mid 40s far eastern areas to\nthe upper 50s far western Sandhills. On Saturday highs from 45\nto 50 and upper 40s to around 50 Sunday. By Monday and Tuesday\nupper ridging will traverse the region with dry conditions and\nhighs returning to the low to mid 50s.",
